Every clinician may elicit a meaningful-functional-goal from a patient.
A meaningful-functional-goal-example includes a dog-walking-example and includes a block-walking-example and includes a part-time-work-return-example and includes a family-event-attendance-example and includes a recreational-activity-attendance-example.
If a clinician elicits a meaningful-functional-goal from a patient then the clinician may use the meaningful-functional-goal during an opioid-benefit-assessment for the patient.
If a clinician elicits a meaningful-functional-goal from a patient then the clinician may use the meaningful-functional-goal during a continued-opioid-benefit-risk-weighing for the patient.
